[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to a Subdomain Takeover vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when user-input subdomain prefixes are not properly validated or restricted, allowing an attacker to create arbitrary subdomains under a trusted domain. If the application constructs URLs using these user inputs without adequate checks, it could lead to scenarios where an attacker can control the subdomain, potentially redirecting users to malicious sites or exploiting the trust associated with the legitimate domain. This occurs because the code does not enforce strict validation on the format or existence of the subdomain, enabling exploitation through crafted inputs.

